  "term": "congenital hypothyroidism",
  "definition": "Congenital hypothyroidism is a condition present in infancy or early childhood caused by too little thyroid hormone before birth. It can result from genetic or environmental causes, including problems in thyroid development, and may lead to major intellectual impairment along with delayed bone growth, short stature, and myxedema.",
